<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0;net11.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <RootNamespace>Sheetwright</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Sheetwright</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Label="Package">
    <PackageId>Sheetwright</PackageId>
    <Description>A small, MIT-licensed .xlsx writer over DocumentFormat.OpenXml, and a streaming reader for the .xlsx and CSV files people upload. Styles, number formats, data validation, conditional formatting, tables, defined names, pictures, freeze panes and auto-fit, a streaming writer for exports too large to hold in memory, and row-at-a-time readers with limits for files from strangers — with a familiar API and no commercial licence.</Description>
    <PackageTags>xlsx;excel;spreadsheet;openxml;export;import;csv;csv-reader;streaming;conditional-formatting</PackageTags>
    <!--
      Shown on nuget.org beside the version. Kept to what changed, in the same
      words as CHANGELOG.md, because a release note that restates the package
      description tells a reader nothing about whether to upgrade.
    -->
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
Added: SpreadsheetWorkbookReader and SpreadsheetCsvReader, which read any .xlsx or CSV file a row at a time, for an import. Dates are recognised by their cell format, a formula is its stored value and is never evaluated, the CSV encoding and separator are detected from the start of the file, and the apostrophe that SpreadsheetGridCsv adds to defuse a formula is taken off again so a file the writer made reads back as the values that went in. Every limit (uncompressed size, compression ratio, shared strings, parts, rows, columns, cell length) is checked while the file is read and refused by name with SpreadsheetReadLimitException; no DTD is processed and nothing outside the package is read.

Changed: net11.0 is a target framework, and the build uses the .NET 11 SDK.

Full notes: https://github.com/sinanoran/sheetwright/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <!--
      CS1591 is off while the public surface is documented incrementally. The
      types that carry a comment carry a real one; turning this into an error
      today would buy fifty stubs saying "Gets or sets the value".
    -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="DocumentFormat.OpenXml" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Sheetwright.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
